<title>USA: Motorola gets contract for western Africa.</title>
<headline>Motorola gets contract for western Africa.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Tuesday its international cellular infrastructure group had been awarded contracts to install separate wireless local loop systems in western Africa.</p>
<p>The contract was awarded by GETESA, the Guinea Equatorial operator for national and international communications, J.V. France Cable Radio, and the Guinea Equatorial government.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
